  "term": "presbycusis",
  "definition": "Presbycusis is age-related hearing loss that usually affects both ears and develops gradually. It is linked to progressive changes in the cochlea and central hearing pathways, often starting with difficulty hearing high-pitched sounds before affecting middle and lower frequencies.",
